        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: The Jargon Society\n- People: Jonathan Williams, Charles Olson, Louis Zukofsky, Paul Metcalf, James Broughton\n- Concepts: American literary avant-garde, Objectivist group of poets\n- Products: White Trash Cooking\n\nFacts:\n- The Jargon Society has published seminal works of the American literary avant-garde.\n- The Jargon Society has published books by Charles Olson, Louis Zukofsky, Paul Metcalf, James Broughton, and Jonathan Williams.\n- The Jargon Society has also published sui generis folk art books such as White Trash Cooking.\n- Louis Zukofsky was one of the founders of the Objectivist group of poets.\n- Louis Zukofsky was the primary theorist of the Objectivist group of poets.\n- Louis Zukofsky influenced subsequent generations of poets in America and abroad.",
